        <div class="row">
            
       <div class="col-lg-8">
             <img class="blog-hero-image" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="SSC MTS Admit Card 2026: Paper-Wise Hall Ticket Download">
             <div class="blog-content">
                <div class="blog-body">
                    <h1 class="blog-title mb-4">SSC MTS Admit Card 2026: Your Essential Guide to Paper-Wise Hall Ticket Download</h1>

                    <p>The Staff Selection Commission (SSC) is all set to conduct the Multi-Tasking (Non-Technical) Staff and Havaldar (CBIC &amp; CBN) Examination 2025, with the Computer-Based Test (CBT) for Paper-I commencing from <span class="highlight-text">February 4, 2026, onwards</span>. For all aspiring candidates, the release of the SSC MTS Admit Card 2026 (for the 2025 recruitment cycle) is a crucial step towards appearing for this highly anticipated examination. This comprehensive guide will walk you through everything you need to know about downloading your hall ticket, understanding key dates, and ensuring a smooth exam experience.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">SSC MTS 2026: Key Dates at a Glance</h2>
                    <p>Staying informed about the important dates is paramount. Here's a quick overview of the essential timelines related to the SSC MTS &amp; Havaldar Examination 2025 being conducted in 2026:</p>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Event</th>
                                <th>Tentative Dates</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td>SSC MTS &amp; Havaldar (2025 Cycle) Exam Dates</td>
                                <td>February 4 – February 15, 2026 (Onwards)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>SSC MTS Self-Slot Booking/City Intimation (2025 Cycle)</td>
                                <td>January 15 – January 25, 2026</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>SSC MTS Admit Card (2025 Cycle) Release</td>
                                <td>From February 1, 2026 onwards (3-4 days before exam)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>SSC MTS 2026 Notification (New Cycle) Expected</td>
                                <td>June 2026</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>SSC MTS 2026 Exam (New Cycle) Expected</td>
                                <td>September - November 2026</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>

                    <h2 class="section-title">How to Download Your SSC MTS Paper-I Hall Ticket 2026</h2>
                    <p>The Staff Selection Commission will release the admit cards on its official website and respective regional portals. Candidates are advised to download their hall tickets well in advance to avoid last-minute technical glitches. Follow these step-by-step instructions to secure your SSC MTS Paper-I Admit Card:</p>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">1. Visit the Official SSC Website</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Navigate to the Staff Selection Commission's official website, <a href="https://ssc.gov.in" target="_blank">www.ssc.gov.in</a>. Alternatively, you can directly visit your respective regional SSC website.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">2. Locate the "Admit Card" Section</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">On the homepage, click on the "Admit Card" tab, usually found in the top navigation bar. This will lead you to a page with links to all regional websites.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">3. Select Your Regional Website</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Click on the link corresponding to the regional office under which you applied for the SSC MTS examination. SSC releases admit cards region-wise.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">4. Find the Admit Card Link</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Look for the notification or link titled "Call Letter for Paper 1 in respect of Multi-Tasking (Non-Technical) Staff and Havaldar (CBIC &amp; CBN) Examination, 2025" or similar for the 2026 examination cycle.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">5. Enter Your Login Credentials</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">You will be prompted to enter your Registration ID or Roll Number, along with your Date of Birth or Password. Ensure these details are entered accurately as provided during your application.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">6. Complete Captcha (if applicable) and Submit</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Enter the security captcha code displayed on the screen and click "Submit".</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">7. Download and Print Your Admit Card</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Your SSC MTS Admit Card 2026 will appear on the screen. Carefully review all the details, then download it and take a clear printout. It is advisable to take multiple printouts, preferably in color.</div>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Important: SSC MTS Self-Slot Booking 2026</h2>
                    <p>For the SSC MTS &amp; Havaldar Examination 2025 (exam in 2026), the Staff Selection Commission introduced a self-slot booking facility. This allowed candidates to choose their preferred exam date, shift, and city from January 15 to January 25, 2026. If you participated in this process, your admit card will reflect your chosen slot. If you did not, a slot would have been automatically assigned to you.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Details to Verify on Your Admit Card</h2>
                    <p>Once you download your SSC MTS Admit Card, it is crucial to meticulously check all the information printed on it. Any discrepancy should be immediately reported to the concerned SSC regional office. Key details to verify include:</p>
                    <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ Candidate's Name</p>
                        <p>✅ Photograph and Signature</p>
                        <p>✅ Roll Number and Registration Number</p>
                        <p>✅ Date and Time of Examination</p>
                        <p>✅ Father's Name</p>
                        <p>✅ Date of Birth</p>
                        <p>✅ Examination Centre Name and Address</p>
                        <p>✅ Reporting Time</p>
                        <p>✅ Exam Day Instructions and Guidelines</p>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Mandatory Documents to Carry to the Exam Centre</h2>
                    <p>On the day of the examination, candidates must carry specific documents to gain entry to the exam hall. Failure to produce these will lead to disqualification. Ensure you have the following:</p>
                    <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ A printed copy of your SSC MTS Paper-I Admit Card 2026 (preferably color)</p>
                        <p>✅ An original, valid photo identification proof (e.g., Aadhaar Card, PAN Card, Voter ID, Driving License, Passport). Ensure the name and details on the ID match your admit card</p>
                        <p>✅ Three recent passport-size photographs, identical to the one uploaded in your application form and printed on the admit card</p>
                        <p>✅ Hand sanitizer and face mask (as per prevailing health guidelines)</p>
                    </div>

                    <p class="highlight-text"><strong>Important Note:</strong> SSC does NOT send admit cards via post or email. Candidates are solely responsible for downloading and printing their hall tickets from the official website.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Final Tips for Exam Day</h2>
                    <p>With your admit card in hand, focus on your final preparations. Arrive at the examination center well before the reporting time mentioned on your admit card. Familiarize yourself with the exam day instructions to avoid any last-minute stress. Good luck to all candidates appearing for the SSC MTS Paper-I Examination 2026!</p>
                </div>
             </div>
       </div>
    
            
